{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Warren County Canal was a branch of the Miami and Erie Canal in southwestern Ohio about 20 mi in length that connected the Warren County seat of Lebanon to the main canal at Middletown in the mid-19th century.","title":"Warren County Canal"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Lebanon was at the crossroads of two major roads, the highway from Cincinnati to Columbus (later U.S. Route 42) and the road from Chillicothe to the College Township (Oxford), but Lebanon businessmen and civic leaders wanted better transportation facilities and successfully lobbied for their own canal, part of the canal fever of the first third of the 19th century.","title":"Warren County Canal"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Warren County Canal was never successful, operating less than a decade before the state abandoned it.","title":"Warren County Canal"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Matton Shipyard is a historic shipyard and canal boat service yard located on Van Schaick Island at Cohoes in Albany County, New York.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It consists of eight extant buildings, various surviving features, and archaeological remains dating to the period 1916 to 1983 when the site functioned as a shipyard, repair facility, and towboat operation on the New York State Barge Canal and Champlain Canal.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Extant buildings include the office / stores (c. 1916-1917), watchman's building (c. 1936-1943), sheet metal shop (c. 1937-1938), carpenter shop (c. 1916 and 1936-1943), stores building (c. 1941-1943), pipeshop (c. 1936-1943), pitch building (pre-1936), garage (c. 1916), and electric building.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Also on the property are a flagpole (c. 1916), dock, steel launching ramps, fence, and camels.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Numerous ruins also occupy the property.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The motor ship "Day Peckinpaugh" is berthed here.","title":"Matton Shipyard"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Route 57 is a state highway located in Warren County in the U.S. state of New Jersey.","title":"New Jersey Route 57"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It runs 21.10 mi from an interchange with U.S. Route 22 (US 22) in Lopatcong Township to an intersection with Route 182 and County Route 517 (CR 517) in Hackettstown.","title":"New Jersey Route 57"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The route passes through mostly rural areas of farmland and mountains in Warren County.","title":"New Jersey Route 57"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It also passes through Washington, where Route 57 crosses Route 31.","title":"New Jersey Route 57"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The route is designated a scenic byway, the Warren Heritage Scenic Byway, by the state of New Jersey due to the physical environments it passes through as well as from historical sites along the way such as the Morris Canal.","title":"New Jersey Route 57"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Albrechtice "(German: Olbersdorf)" is a village in the Pardubice Region of the Czech Republic.","title":"Albrechtice (Ústí nad Orlicí District)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located 3 km northeast of Lanškroun and had a population of 497 in 2006.","title":"Albrechtice (Ústí nad Orlicí District)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is not to be confused with the much larger town of the same names (both Czech and German) located farther east, in the Moravian portion of the Czech Republic.","title":"Albrechtice (Ústí nad Orlicí District)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Designed by Frank Lloyd Wright in 1953 and completed in 1954, the John and Syd Dobkins House is one of three Wright-designed Usonian houses in Canton, Ohio.","title":"John and Syd Dobkins House"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Located farther east than the Nathan Rubin Residence and the Ellis A. Feiman House, it is set back from the road, has tall, thin casement windows and prominent doors that rise to nearly the roofline.","title":"John and Syd Dobkins House"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Its distinctive geometric design module based upon an equilateral triangle reflects Wright's Usonian design philosophy.","title":"John and Syd Dobkins House"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Warren County School District (WCSD) is a public school district in Warren County, Pennsylvania, and it is designed to encompass all but three county municipalities.","title":"Warren County School District"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It has four attendance areas: North, East, West and Central.","title":"Warren County School District"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Warren County School District encompasses approximately 792 square miles.","title":"Warren County School District"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" According to 2000 federal census data, it serves a resident population of 40,689.","title":"Warren County School District"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 2009, the residents' per capita income was $17,898, while median family income was $42,714.","title":"Warren County School District"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In the Commonwealth, the median family income was","title":"Warren County School District"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Champlain Canal
